{"id": "3f32a761-b1e6-4753-b5bb-53d761170970", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll run this through the CloudFront operational review methodology — a multi-pass scan across all your distributions covering security (TLS, WAF, origin access), performance (caching), operational excellence (logging, alarms), and cost. Since this involves a lot of API calls across distributions, policies, WAF, ACM, CloudWatch, and Cost Explorer, I'll have this researched thoroughly in the background rather than pulling all that raw data into our chat.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_qprAVdGjxFfOmSSqbJNbt2", "tool_name": "gather_context", "input": {"deep_research": true, "prompt": "{
  "task": "Run the cloudfront-operation-review skill end-to-end against this AWS account and produce the full operational review report.",
  "context": "User asked: 'Run an operational review of my CloudFront distributions. Check TLS, WAF, origin access, caching, logging and cost, and rate each finding by severity.' This is a proactive posture review, not an incident investigation. Use skill_id 'cloudfront-operation-review' via skill_read to load SKILL.md and follow it exactly: discover distributions and shared edge resources (Pass 1), score/rank, do Pass 2 deep-dive reads (metrics, WAF, ACM, cost) for the ranked set, evaluate remaining checks against the best-practices checklist, apply severity/scoring reference, and generate the final report per the report template. Load all referenced resource files (origin-classification.md, best-practices-checklist.md, metrics-thresholds.md, severity-and-scoring.md, report-template.md) as instructed by the skill.",
  "resources": ["AWS account 012345678901_1, all CloudFront distributions in it, us-east-1 control-plane calls as the skill requires (CloudFront is global but APIs are called in us-east-1)"],
  "timeframe": "Use the skill's default 7-day metric window for Pass 2 CloudWatch queries",
  "criteria": "Scope: all distributions, all five pillars (security, reliability, performance, operational-excellence, cost) since the user asked for TLS, WAF, origin access, caching, logging, and cost coverage. Rate every finding by severity (CRITICAL/HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW/INFO) per the severity-and-scoring reference. Include: distribution inventory, findings by pillar with check IDs, metrics summary, visibility limits (any denied calls, disabled monitoring subscriptions, unavailable cost data), readiness score, and prioritized Current→Risk→Fix recommendations citing CloudFront docs. Report back the full structured findings (executive summary, scores, per-distribution findings, visibility limits, recommendations) so I can present them to the user — do not just say a report was created, return the actual content and severities."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Run a full CloudFront operational review across distributions in this account."}], "created_at": null}

